Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 18:29:56 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] libeffects: Make the AIDL effect libraries visible to the
 mainline audio HAL

The AIDL effect plugin libraries built here (libbundleaidl, libreverbaidl,
libdownmixaidl, libdynamicsprocessingaidl, liberaser and its model files,
libhapticgeneratoraidl, libloudnessenhanceraidl, libpreprocessingaidl,
libvisualizeraidl) restrict their visibility to
//hardware/interfaces/audio/aidl/default and its subpackages, since the
only consumer so far was the example APEX com.android.hardware.audio.

The generic alsa-lib based audio HAL for mainline kernels lives in
hardware/mainline/common/interfaces/audio/mainline and ships its own
vendor APEX. It reuses the unmodified example effect service and needs
to bundle these plugin libraries into that APEX, which Soong rejects as
long as the package is not listed in the visibility of every library.

Add the mainline HAL package to the visibility list of each library. No
other change; the libraries themselves are untouched.

Assisted-by: OpenCode/anthropic/claude-fable-5-1
Change-Id: Idaf17c8bc6454064bbc1f0f15f0caa6772bdb2f3
